🛡️ Layer 0: Global Security Hardening
Before adding new features, we must secure the existing infrastructure.

Rate Limiting: Implement AspNetCoreRateLimit on the backend to prevent brute-force attacks on Login, OTP Verification, and 

Registration
 endpoints.
Security Headers: Configure Middleware to inject Content-Security-Policy (CSP), X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS).
Encrypted Storage: Ensure sensitive files (NID copies, proof of payments) are stored in a non-public directory with access strictly controlled via the 

IMemberService
.
Audit Logging: Expand the AuditLogMiddleware to track every modification in the Financial Ledger and Payment Configurations, recording the AdminEmail, IPAddress, and FieldChanges.

📅 Phase 1: Communication & Identity (Foundation)
Focus: Enhancing the member's first impression and verifying identity.

Verified Digital ID Card:
Enhance IIDCardService to generate a PDF with an embedded QR Code.
Security Enhancement: The QR code should point to a public-but-obfuscated URL (e.g., /verify/alumni/{hash}) that allows reunion security staff to verify membership without exposing the full profile.
Rich Email Templating:
Integrate Handlebars.Net or RazorEngine for dynamic emails.
Automate "Membership Welcome" emails containing the Digital ID and login credentials.

💳 Phase 2: Payment & SignalR Automation (Efficiency)
Focus: Removing manual verification steps and enabling real-time feedback.

Payment Webhooks:
Implement Callback URLs for SSLCommerz and bKash Gateway.
Security Enhancement: Use HMAC Signature Verification on all incoming payment webhooks to ensure they genuinely come from the payment provider.
SignalR Notification Hub:
Create a NotificationHub to push "Instant Approval" alerts to users.
Admin Side: Real-time "Toast" notifications when a donation over a certain threshold is received.

🤝 Phase 3: The "Haragangian Hub" (Engagement)
Focus: Building value for the alumni and professional networking.

Professional Directory:
Build a searchable database with filters for Batch, Designation, and Industry.
Security Enhancement: Implement Privacy Settings allowing members to hide their Mobile/Email from the public directory while still being "contactable" via an internal messaging system.
Job Referral Portal:
A clean interface for alumni to post vacancies.
Integration with the news/announcements system to highlight major career moves of alumni.

📊 Phase 4: Mobile & Executive Intelligence
Focus: Accessibility and data-driven governance.

PWA Integration:
Add a manifest.json and ServiceWorker to the Angular app.
Enable Offline Mode for the "My ID Card" feature so members can show it even without internet at reunion venues.
Executive Dashboard (EC Module):
Interactive charts showing Batch Distribution, Geographical Hotspots (where do most alumni live?), and Fundraising Velocity.
Admin 2FA: Require TOTP (Google Authenticator) for any admin accessing the "Financial Reports" or "Member Export" features.

